    "labelChirho": "Sheva (proper name)",
    "descriptionChirho": "A Hebrew proper name (שֶׁבַע) referring to: (1) a scribe/secretary under King David (2 Sam 20:25), and (2) a son of Caleb by his concubine Maacah (1 Chr 2:49). All 9 occurrences denote the same proper noun; the two clusters differ only in the presence/absence of the conjunction waw ('and Sheva' vs. 'Sheva'), which is a grammatical surface variation, not a semantic distinction. Evidence: eng 'Sheva / and Sheva,' spa 'Sheva / y Seba,' arb 'شَبَعَ / وَ شابَع,' kor '세바 / 세바,' swa 'Sheba / na Sheba,' hin 'शेबा / और शेबा.' All translations consistently render the same proper noun.",
